        "step_number": 5,
        "text": "Step 5: Find the corresponding \\( y \\)-values for each \\( x \\)-value by substituting back into \\( y = x^2 - 8 \\):\nFor \\( x = \\frac{-5 + \\sqrt{233}}{2} \\):\n\\[ y = \\left( \\frac{-5 + \\sqrt{233}}{2} \\right)^2 - 8 \\]\n\\[ y = \\frac{(-5 + \\sqrt{233})^2}{4} - 8 \\]\n\\[ y = \\frac{25 - 10\\sqrt{233} + 233}{4} - 8 \\]\n\\[ y = \\frac{258 - 10\\sqrt{233}}{4} - 8 \\]\n\\[ y = \\frac{258 - 10\\sqrt{233} - 32}{4} \\]\n\\[ y = \\frac{226 - 10\\sqrt{233}}{4} \\]\n\\[ y = \\frac{113 - 5\\sqrt{233}}{2} \\]\n\nFor \\( x = \\frac{-5 - \\sqrt{233}}{2} \\):\n\\[ y = \\left( \\frac{-5 - \\sqrt{233}}{2} \\right)^2 - 8 \\]\n\\[ y = \\frac{(-5 - \\sqrt{233})^2}{4} - 8 \\]\n\\[ y = \\frac{25 + 10\\sqrt{233} + 233}{4} - 8 \\]\n\\[ y = \\frac{258 + 10\\sqrt{233}}{4} - 8 \\]\n\\[ y = \\frac{258 + 10\\sqrt{233} - 32}{4} \\]\n\\[ y = \\frac{226 + 10\\sqrt{233}}{4} \\]\n\\[ y = \\frac{113 + 5\\sqrt{233}}{2} \\]"
      },
