  "raw_text": "Step 1: Set the two expressions for \\( y \\) equal to each other since they both represent \\( y \\):\n\\[ x^2 - 8 = y^2 \\]\n\nStep 2: Substitute \\( y^2 \\) from the second equation into the first equation:\n\\[ x^2 - 8 = -5x + 44 \\]\n\nStep 3: Rearrange the equation to form a standard quadratic equation:\n\\[ x^2 + 5x - 52 = 0 \\]\n\nStep 4: Solve the quadratic equation using the quadratic formula \\( x = \\frac{-b \\pm \\sqrt{b^2 - 4ac}}{2a} \\), where \\( a = 1 \\), \\( b = 5 \\), and \\( c = -52 \\):\n\\[ x = \\frac{-5 \\pm \\sqrt{5^2 - 4 \\cdot 1 \\cdot (-52)}}{2 \\cdot 1} \\]\n\\[ x = \\frac{-5 \\pm \\sqrt{25 + 208}}{2} \\]\n\\[ x = \\frac{-5 \\pm \\sqrt{233}}{2} \\]\n\nStep 5: Find the corresponding \\( y \\)-values for each \\( x \\)-value by substituting back into \\( y = x^2 - 8 \\):\nFor \\( x = \\frac{-5 + \\sqrt{233}}{2} \\):\n\\[ y = \\left( \\frac{-5 + \\sqrt{233}}{2} \\right)^2 - 8 \\]\n\\[ y = \\frac{(-5 + \\sqrt{233})^2}{4} - 8 \\]\n\\[ y = \\frac{25 - 10\\sqrt{233} + 233}{4} - 8 \\]\n\\[ y = \\frac{258 - 10\\sqrt{233}}{4} - 8 \\]\n\\[ y = \\frac{258 - 10\\sqrt{233} - 32}{4} \\]\n\\[ y = \\frac{226 - 10\\sqrt{233}}{4} \\]\n\\[ y = \\frac{113 - 5\\sqrt{233}}{2} \\]\n\nFor \\( x = \\frac{-5 - \\sqrt{233}}{2} \\):\n\\[ y = \\left( \\frac{-5 - \\sqrt{233}}{2} \\right)^2 - 8 \\]\n\\[ y = \\frac{(-5 - \\sqrt{233})^2}{4} - 8 \\]\n\\[ y = \\frac{25 + 10\\sqrt{233} + 233}{4} - 8 \\]\n\\[ y = \\frac{258 + 10\\sqrt{233}}{4} - 8 \\]\n\\[ y = \\frac{258 + 10\\sqrt{233} - 32}{4} \\]\n\\[ y = \\frac{226 + 10\\sqrt{233}}{4} \\]\n\\[ y = \\frac{113 + 5\\sqrt{233}}{2} \\]\n\nStep 6: Calculate the product of the \\( y \\)-values:\n\\[ \\left( \\frac{113 - 5\\sqrt{233}}{2} \\right) \\left( \\frac{113 + 5\\sqrt{233}}{2} \\right) \\]\n\\[ = \\frac{(113 - 5\\sqrt{233})(113 + 5\\sqrt{233})}{4} \\]\n\\[ = \\frac{113^2 - (5\\sqrt{233})^2}{4} \\]\n\\[ = \\frac{12769 - 5750}{4} \\]\n\\[ = \\frac{7019}{4} \\]\n\nFinal answer: \\boxed{\\frac{7019}{4}}<|im_end